        "nobel_worthiness": "Atomic-resolution qPlus force microscopy opened a powerful route to imaging and measuring local forces at the atomic scale.",
        "attribution": "Giessibl developed the qPlus sensor and its key microscopy method; Meyer and Gross contributed important demonstrations and extensions of atomic-scale imaging and chemical identification.",
        "maturity": "The technique has been used and refined for many years, with strong experimental validation across a range of surfaces and molecules.",
